@startuml
skinparam componentStyle rectangle
skinparam wrapWidth 200
skinparam maxMessageSize 200

title Java HTTP Proxy System with Bundled Test Utilities

package "External Clients" {
  cloud "HTTP Client\n(external)" as ExtClient
}

package "Proxy Module (Java)" {
  component "HTTP Proxy" as Proxy
  component "Upstream Channel Adapter\n(Netty)" as NettyAdapter
  Proxy -[hidden]down- NettyAdapter
}

package "Upstream Server (external)" {
  cloud "Upstream Server" as Upstream
}

package "Test Server Module\n(Grizzly/Jersey)" {
  node "Test Server" as TestServer {
    component "REST API" as RestAPI
    component "Download Endpoint\nGET /download" as DownloadEP
    component "Upload Handler\nreturns map{filepath -> filename}" as UploadEP
  }
  database "Local File System" as FileSystem
  DownloadEP --> FileSystem : read target file\n(C-004)
  RestAPI -[hidden]- DownloadEP
  RestAPI -[hidden]- UploadEP
}

package "Test Client Module" {
  node "Test Client" as TestClient {
    component "Workload Runner\nFixed Thread Pool" as Workload
    component "Async HTTP Client" as AsyncClient
    component "Success Counter" as SuccessCounter
  }
  Workload --> AsyncClient : schedule async GETs\n(C-003)
  AsyncClient --> SuccessCounter : increment on HTTP 200\n(FR-006, DR-006)
}

rectangle "Structured Response Object\n{ code: Integer, msg: String, data: Object }" as StructuredResponse

' Primary HTTP flow through proxy
ExtClient --> Proxy : HTTP request\n(URI, headers, body)\n(COM-001, DEF-001)
Proxy --> Upstream : Forward retained FullHttpRequest\n(after upstream channel active)\n(FR-002, FR-003, C-002)
Proxy .. NettyAdapter : uses Netty channel\n(writeAndFlush on activation)

' Test client traffic (can target proxy path or test server directly)
AsyncClient --> Proxy : HTTP GET workload\n(as configured)
AsyncClient --> TestServer : HTTP GETs to base URI\n(FR-001, API-001)

' Test server endpoints and behaviors
ExtClient --> TestServer : HTTP requests\n(COM-001)
AsyncClient --> DownloadEP : GET /download\n(API-003, FR-004, FR-005)
DownloadEP --> AsyncClient : 200 + application/octet-stream\n+ Content-Disposition: attachment; filename=...\n(if file exists)\n(COM-002, DEF-004, DR-003, DR-004)
DownloadEP --> AsyncClient : 404/204 (no file payload)\n(no Content-Disposition)\n(if file absent)\n(FR-005)

AsyncClient --> UploadEP : file upload
UploadEP --> AsyncClient : map payload { filepath: <fileName> }\n(API-004, FR-007, DEF-005, DR-005)

' Structured response usage (generic responses)
TestServer ..> StructuredResponse : returns structured responses\n(DEF-003)
Upstream ..> StructuredResponse : may return structured responses\n(DEF-003)
Proxy ..> StructuredResponse : passes through without modification\n(FR-003)

' Notes and constraints
note right of Proxy
- Forwards retained FullHttpRequest (URI, headers, body)
- No header/body modification required (FR-003)
- Debug logging (when enabled) exposes URI, headers, body (NFR-002)
- Forwards only after upstream Netty channel activation (C-002)
end note

note top of TestServer
- Programmatic startup exposes base URI (FR-001, API-001)
- Grizzly/Jersey HTTP server stack (C-001)
- GET /download returns binary attachment when file exists (FR-004)
- No attachment payload if file absent (FR-005)
end note

note right of DownloadEP
- Content-Type: application/octet-stream
- Content-Disposition includes filename on success (COM-002, DR-004)
- Depends on file existence in Local File System (C-004)
end note

note bottom of TestClient
- Workload: 50 threads x 1,000 async GETs = 50,000 total (NFR-001)
- Success counter increments on HTTP 200 only (FR-006)
- Releases resources: shutdown executor, close async client (NFR-003)
end note

note bottom
Build & Compatibility:
- Maven multi-module baseline (C-005)
- Java targets: root/test-server Java 1.8; proxy SDK Java 1.7 (NFR-004)
- Test server baseline compatible with declared Jersey version (C-006)
end note

@enduml
